      "writtenOn": "2019-11-14T18:56:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure.\n\nNo, it is mainly to clump all the behavior settings into one block, so that a fuzzer can memcpy the random bytes into it.\nSecondly, it is nice to be able to simply reset all the behavior settings by setting one global struct to the reset macro. For example setting the control struct to MOCK_CTRL_DEFAULT_FP_SENSOR from https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/master/include/mock/fp_sensor_mock.h#30 .\n\nI suppose, the name-spacing is another strong benefit.",
